augur (0.2.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The package is augur-dbus: Debian and Ubuntu have an unrelated augur
    (Nextstrain's), with its own /usr/bin/augur. augur-dbus takes over
    from Augur's own augur packages.
  * An apt repository, signed, for Debian 12 and 13 and Ubuntu 24.04.

 -- Matthew Phillips <matthew@matthewphillips.info>  Tue, 06 Oct 2026 19:50:21 -0400

augur (0.2.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * D-Bus: Augur is org.gemwm.Augur, its object /org/gemwm/Augur and its
    interface org.gemwm.Augur1; the io.github.matthewp names are gone.
  * Packages for FreeBSD 14 and 15, from a signed repository.
  * Where GLib can't watch files, augurd looks at its config twice a
    second, so changes to it still take effect.

 -- Matthew Phillips <matthew@matthewphillips.info>  Tue, 06 Oct 2026 18:59:05 -0400

